  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing had total federal contract obligations of $74.9M in FY2027 to date. FY2027 to date totals are partial. Obligations fell 99.5% year over year. The federal government made 244 awards in the NAICS 325412 market so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $307K. FY22 through FY26 show much larger annual obligations: FY22 was $34.4B, FY23 was $12.8B, FY24 was $10.1B, FY25 was $13.1B, and FY26 was $14.5B. The Department of Veterans Affairs accounted for $70.6M of FY2027 to date obligations. The Department of Justice accounted for $4.3M of FY2027 to date obligations. CARDINAL HEALTH 414, LLC received $14.6M so far in FY2027 to date, PROGENICS PHARMACEUTICALS INC received $12.1M, and NOVARTIS PHARMACEUTICALS CORPORATION received $8.4M. Other named vendors with FY2027 to date obligations include EXELAN PHARMACEUTICALS INC ($5.5M), OPTUM INFUSION SERVICES 308, LLC ($4.8M), and MCKESSON CORPORATION ($4.2M).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are FY2027 obligations within the market?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer with $70.6M in FY2027 to date obligations. The Department of Justice is the next largest buyer with $4.3M in FY2027 to date obligations. CARDINAL HEALTH 414, LLC received $14.6M in FY2027 to date and PROGENICS PHARMACEUTICALS INC received $12.1M in FY2027 to date, indicating concentration among top suppliers at the vendor level."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 to date compare with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY2027 to date obligations are $74.9M, a sharp change from prior full fiscal years: FY26 was $14.5B, FY25 was $13.1B, FY24 was $10.1B, FY23 was $12.8B, and FY22 was $34.4B. Obligations fell 99.5% year over year. The count of FY2027 to date awards is 244 with an average award size of $307K."
      }
    ]
  },
